  "title": "# Build: menu-scroll (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"The application menus need to be …",
  "asked": "# Build: menu-scroll (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): \"The application menus need to be scrollable when they reach beyond the screen.\" Assigned agent: **Janitor Joey** (book on his agent-swarm card; set AXF_AGENT=janitor-joey if supported, else record in report + store note). Register in Urgent (id `menu-scroll`) + banner entry. ## Fix (framework level, so every app and plugin gets it) - Application menu bar dropdowns, their submenus, and also context menus / overflow (⋯) menus: when a menu is taller than the space left in the viewport, cap its height to the available space (respect safe-area insets, the banner/toolbars, and the on-screen keyboard; use visualViewport on mobile) and make it scroll vertically inside. - Smooth touch scrolling on phones (overscroll contained so the page behind doesn't scroll), wheel + keyboard arrow navigation scrolls the highlighted item into view, subtle top/bottom fade or chevron hints when there's more. - Positioning: flip up / shift to stay on screen before falling back to scroll; submenus that would go off the right edge open to the left; on compact width they stay inside the screen. - Max height + hint style come from tokens/assets (menu asset or component-sizing), no hard-coded sizes (check-theme must pass). - Apply in the framework menu components (web reference + axf.css) so console, axHub web, AmberX (Capacitor) and every plugin inherit it; Compose twin recorded in PORTING.md unless trivial. - Tests (overflow cases: long menu at bottom of a short phone screen, nested submenu at the edge, keyboard open), before/after screenshots at 412 px and 1280 px, UI Review item, report `_claude/builds/reports/menu-scroll.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
